From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: office <office@localhost>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:47:34 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] deckcraft-web: add an opt-in postMessage host bridge
 (?host=parent)

A page that frames DeckCraft in an <iframe> (the web shell) can now open a presentation in it,
ask it to save, and hear about unsaved changes, the way the WordCraft, GridCraft and PDFCraft web
apps allow for their embedders.

Messages are plain objects with a `type` (the WordCraft bridge's, with the `deckcraft:` prefix):
  deckcraft:ready       (to host)   {version}
  deckcraft:open        (from host) {name, bytes}
  deckcraft:opened      (to host)   {name}
  deckcraft:requestSave (from host)
  deckcraft:save        (to host)   {name, bytes}, bytes transferred; a Save is always a .pptx
  deckcraft:dirty       (to host)   {dirty}
  deckcraft:failed      (to host)   {error}

Only the parent window is heard or answered, and only on its origin: the page's own, or the one
named by &parent_origin=. Without ?host=parent, or without a parent, nothing changes. In host mode
the page starts with a blank presentation instead of the sample deck.
